title: Galleon Fleet II
subtitle: A political question
tags: event
on-arrival: panzerkreuzer_b_seen = 1
new-page: true
face-image: img/panzerkreuzer.jpg
view-if: panzerkreuzer_b_seen = 0 and year = 1931 and month >= 2 and (marcher_in_government = 1 or marcher_toleration = 1) and panzerkreuser_right_seen = 0

= Galleon Fleet II

The Navy is demanding the construction of another new war-galleon. [? if panzerkreuzer_funded: The previous war-galleon had been funded, and has already been launched. Another ship would further progress the Commonwealth's rearmament. ?][? if not panzerkreuzer_funded: The previous war-galleon requested by the Navy was not funded, thanks to us. The military remains bitter, but nevertheless they are still pursuing their rearmament plan, and must seek funding from the Assembly. ?]

Much of our party is deeply opposed to rearmament, while the center and right parties are united in support. What will we do?

- @vote_yes: Vote yes, for constructing the war-galleon.
- @vote_no: Vote no, against constructing the war-galleon.
- @abstain: Abstain from the vote.
- @ministry: Use the Commonwealth Army Ministry to prevent the construction.

@vote_yes
on-arrival: left_dissent += 10; labor_dissent += 5; center_dissent += 5; reformist_dissent += 5 if not panzerkreuzer_funded; knight_dissent += 5 if not panzerkreuzer_funded; panzerkreuzer_b_funded = 1; collectivist_coalition_dissent += 1; collectivist_relation -= 6; commons_marcher -= 4; gold_left += 1; dufour_angry -= 5; military_confidence += 1; lvp_relation += 2

Our grassroots party members are highly critical of our decision. Many party branches have increased their agitation against our parliamentary fraction. [? if panzerkreuzer_funded : However, given the construction of the previous war-galleon, this seemed to be a foregone conclusion, and the reaction is muted. ?]

The vote in favor of the war-galleon easily passes, with opposition only from the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>. The ship will be built.

@vote_no
on-arrival: gold_relation -= 8; lvp_relation -= 2; unionist_relation -= 5; pacifism += 1; nationalism -= 5*(1-dissent); coalition_dissent += 1; commons_marcher += 4*(1-dissent) if nationalism < 49; gold_right += 1; dufour_angry += 5; military_confidence -= 1 if military_confidence > 0
go-to: built if marcher_r + collectivist_r + sapd_r < 50; not_built if marcher_r + collectivist_r + sapd_r >= 50

Our vote against the war-galleon is unpopular among the right-wing parties[? if in_grand_coalition or in_weimar_coalition: , including our coalition partners ?][? if marcher_toleration: , including the minority government that we are currently supporting ?].

@abstain
on-arrival: gold_relation -= 5; unionist_relation -= 3; left_dissent += 5; labor_dissent += 5 if not panzerkreuzer_funded; panzerkreuzer_b_funded = 1; collectivist_relation -= 3

The center-right parties are critical of our decision to abstain, and the pressure from our left flank is not entirely assuaged. Despite our abstention, the vote in the Assembly passes, with all parties in favor except the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> and <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>. The ship will be built.

[? if panzerkreuzer_funded : Given the construction of the previous war-galleon, this seemed to be a foregone conclusion, and the reaction is muted. ?]

@built
on-arrival: panzerkreuzer_b_funded = 1

Chancellor [+ chancellor +] brings the matter to a full Assembly vote, which passes with all parties in favor except the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> and <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>. The ship will be built.

@not_built
on-arrival: panzerkreuzer_b_funded = 0; budget += 1 if panzerkreuzer_funded = 0; dufour_angry += 5; coup_progress += 1

Our vote against the war-galleon succeeds, with the support of the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>. The ship will not be built! [? if panzerkreuzer_funded == 0 : We have saved some budget from not funding the two ships. ?]

@ministry
on-arrival: panzerkreuzer_b_funded = 0; budget += 1 if panzerkreuzer_funded = 0; dufour_angry += 5; coup_progress += 1
view-if: army_minister_party == "Marcher"

With our control of the Commonwealth Army Ministry, we have pressured the Navy to abandon its rearmament plans. The ship will not be built. [? if panzerkreuzer_funded == 0 : We have saved some budget from not funding the two ships. ?]
